# PanCyto retrieval task set (30 tasks)
#
# CORPUS: /dartfs/rc/nosnapshots/V/VaickusL-nb/EDIT_Interns_2026/projects/PanCyto
#   Indexed:  scripts/ configs/ notebooks/   (.py .ipynb .yaml .sh .sbatch)
#   Excluded: corpus/ eval/ runs/ extraction/ compare*/ test_slides/ third_party/
#
#   Why those exclusions:
#     - eval/train_files.txt and eval/eval_holdout_slides.txt are slide-ID lists.
#       .txt is in the indexer's default extension set, so indexing them would put
#       patient identifiers into the vector store.
#     - compare*/ filenames (469506_RGB.png etc.) look like accession numbers, and
#       chunk_text() stamps the file path into every chunk, so paths leak too.
#     - runs/*/config.yaml are near-duplicate snapshots of configs/*.yaml. Including
#       them would make several comprehend answers ambiguous across 7 files.
#
# GROUND TRUTH STATUS: DRAFT, NOT YET HUMAN-VERIFIED.
#   comprehend/* values were read directly out of the files and are high confidence.
#   locate/* answers derive from each script's own docstring.
#   undocumented/* were verified absent by grep across scripts/ configs/ notebooks/
#     (checked: consent, journal, "submitted to", "patient age", demographic,
#      institution, hospital, funding -> 0 files each).
#     NOTE: IRB, protocol, kappa, and cost DO appear in the corpus and were
#     rejected as controls for that reason.
#
#   Before any result is reported, ground_truth_source must be updated to name the
#   human who confirmed each item. Aaditya (PanCyto owner) should review locate/*.
